                <pb facs="0363" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.842/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-08T17:00:00+03:00">July 8, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>461. I have received a written order from His Excellency, Marshal Graziani, that
                    in view of the situation which has developed since my interview with him, he
                    finds himself obliged to close for a period of <pb facs="0364" n="299"
                        xml:id="pg299"/> 15 days the radio stations of the four Legations possessing
                    them. I have complied with his request but have obtained authorization to
                    continue to receive messages. Beginning today I shall therefore send my messages
                    via Italian radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
